// Chapter 1, Mr. Fins the loan shark.
// Every option runs <<choose "id">>; its effects live in Content/storylets_ch1.json.
// Russian text lives in Story-ru.csv; keep #line ids stable.

title: ch1_shark_offer
---
A shark in a pinstripe suit leans against your building. His smile has too many rows. #line:ch1_shark_offer_01
Mr. Fins: Rough month? I can help. A thousand dollars, right now, no paperwork. #line:ch1_shark_offer_02
Mr. Fins: You pay back thirteen hundred in two months. Easy. #line:ch1_shark_offer_03
-> Take the thousand. #line:ch1_shark_offer_04
    <<choose "take">>
    Mr. Fins: Pleasure doing business. I'll find you. I always do. #line:ch1_shark_offer_05
-> No thanks. #line:ch1_shark_offer_06
    <<choose "refuse">>
    Mr. Fins: The offer swims by again. They always do. #line:ch1_shark_offer_07
===

title: ch1_shark_apr
---
Unpaid CEO: Three hundred on a thousand for two months. Do the math with me. #line:ch1_shark_apr_01
Unpaid CEO: That's fifteen percent a month. Over a year, a hundred and eighty percent. A credit card is around twenty-two. #line:ch1_shark_apr_02
Unpaid CEO: Sharks don't sell money. They sell time, at the worst possible price. #line:ch1_shark_apr_03
-> Pay him back as fast as I can. #line:ch1_shark_apr_04
    <<choose "repay_fast">>
    Unpaid CEO: Good. Interest is a race you only win by quitting early. #line:ch1_shark_apr_05
-> It's just one loan. Relax. #line:ch1_shark_apr_06
    <<choose "relax">>
    Unpaid CEO: That's what everyone says before the second one. #line:ch1_shark_apr_07
===

title: ch1_shark_collect
---
Mr. Fins: Two months. Clock's up. Thirteen hundred. #line:ch1_shark_collect_01
-> Pay in full. #line:ch1_shark_collect_02
    <<choose "pay">>
    Mr. Fins: Clean. I like clean. #line:ch1_shark_collect_03
-> Pay two hundred interest and beg for more time. #line:ch1_shark_collect_04
    <<choose "extend">>
    Mr. Fins: Two more months. The thirteen hundred doesn't shrink, kid. #line:ch1_shark_collect_05
-> Refuse to pay. #line:ch1_shark_collect_06
    <<choose "refuse">>
    Mr. Fins: Wrong answer. We'll talk again. Soon. #line:ch1_shark_collect_07
===

title: ch1_shark_threat
---
Your delivery bike is gone. In its place, a business card with a fin on it. #line:ch1_shark_threat_01
Mr. Fins: Fifteen hundred and you get the bike back. Or enjoy walking. #line:ch1_shark_threat_02
-> Pay the fifteen hundred. #line:ch1_shark_threat_03
    <<choose "pay">>
    Mr. Fins: See? We're friends again. #line:ch1_shark_threat_04
-> Let the bike go. The debt is settled. #line:ch1_shark_threat_05
    <<choose "let_go">>
    Mr. Fins: Fair trade. Nice bike, by the way. #line:ch1_shark_threat_06
===

title: ch1_shark_job
---
Mr. Fins: You paid on time. That makes you rare. I could use a reliable face. #line:ch1_shark_job_01
Mr. Fins: Collections. You knock, they pay, you keep ten percent. #line:ch1_shark_job_02
-> Take the job. #line:ch1_shark_job_03
    <<choose "accept">>
    The money is fast. The looks on people's faces stay with you longer. #line:ch1_shark_job_04
-> Not my kind of business. #line:ch1_shark_job_05
    <<choose "decline">>
    Mr. Fins: Principles. Expensive hobby. #line:ch1_shark_job_06
===
